.TH CDCSTORE 7 "October 2026" "cdcstore" "Miscellaneous"
.SH NAME
cdcstore \- a repository of files cut into chunks, with an index
.SH DESCRIPTION
cdcstore keeps files as chunks, one chunk per file, with a single index. It prepares data for an archiver; it does not compress, deduplicate or pack anything itself. Finding what repeats is the job of the sorter (sortof\-cdcsort) and the container (tar and zstd, zfrag, DwarFS and so on). Adding or removing one item is one command, so a collection that has to fit a disc can be adjusted one file at a time.
.SH THE REPOSITORY
A repository is a directory:
.PP
.nf
.RS
cdcstore.idx                      the index, rewritten atomically after every change
chunks/bNNNNN/cNNNNNNNNN             every chunk as its own file, raw bytes, 5000 per bucket folder
.RE
.fi
.sp
Chunks are numbered in the order they first appear, so the natural order of the chunk files is the order the data was added. A chunk belongs to one file and never spans two files. Numbers are never reused, so removing a file does not rename any other chunk and a list that was already sorted or archived stays valid.
.PP
The index is little endian, every section starts on an eight\-byte boundary and every table is a plain array of packed records, so a mount can map it and use it as it is. It holds a header (magic CDCSTOR1, version, sizes, a checksum), the chunk table, the entries sorted by path (so a lookup is a binary search and a folder is followed by everything inside it), the chunk list of every file with its offsets, and the path strings. The full layout is described at the top of cdcstore\-common.h in the source.
.SH PROGRAMS
cdcstore\-add stores files, cdcstore\-remove takes them out, cdcstore\-restore restores them, cdcstore\-list lists them (and prints the chunk list with \-k), cdcstore\-verify checks them, and cdcstore\-mount mounts the repository read\-only.
.SH TO AN ARCHIVE
.nf
.RS
cdcstore\-list \-k REPO | sortof\-cdcsort \- > list.txt
zfrag pack \-T list.txt \-o set.tar.zfrag
.RE
.fi
.sp
Anything that restores from the archive needs all the chunk files of the files it restores. zfrag mount shows the files a repository inside an archive holds, under virtual/, without extracting it.
